# D51 / `todo/t0718` — `unify`'s smart-pointer coercion is keyed on the TYPED
# builtin IDENTITY (`DefInfo.builtin_kind`), never on the definition's NAME.
#
# ⛔ THIS ROW IS THE POINT OF THE WHOLE SET. Every reject row above passes if
# the identity is NEVER SEEDED — a migration that wires the accessor and forgets
# the seed rejects everything and looks perfect. These accept rows are what
# distinguish "keyed on the typed flag" from "the flag is always `None`".
#
# ⚠ `check`-ONLY, DELIBERATELY. This shape is accepted and then MISCOMPILES:
# the call passes the bare `int` where the callee's ABI wants a pointer
# (`-Wint-conversion`) and the program SIGSEGVs. That is a PRE-EXISTING lowering
# defect on the BUILTIN path — measured identical before and after this
# migration, which touches no lowering — filed as `todo/t1527` with a
# `known_gaps` repro. Do not promote these rows to `run_gg` until it is fixed.
#
# SEAM: seed site A, second name — `Mutex`.
# Asserted by `coercion_identity_builtin_mutex_still_coerces`.

void worker(Mutex[int] c):
    print(1)

void main():
    shared int counter = 0
    worker(counter)
